🚨 Solved SQL Noir Case #006 — The Vanishing Diamond 💎

Just completed another SQL detective investigation where data analysis and logical querying uncovered the thief behind a luxury diamond heist.

🕵️ The Case:
At Miami’s prestigious Fontainebleau Hotel charity gala, the legendary “Heart of Atlantis” diamond necklace suddenly disappeared from its display.

The investigation began by analyzing the crime scene report and witness statements.

🔍 Witness Clues:
• Someone mentioned meeting at marina dock 3
• The suspect carried an invitation ending with “-R”
• The suspect wore a navy suit with a white tie

Using SQL, I investigated multiple relational tables and gradually narrowed down the suspects through filtering and JOIN operations.

🧠 SQL Concepts Used:
✔️ WHERE filtering
✔️ LIKE operators
✔️ INNER JOIN
✔️ DISTINCT
✔️ Multi-table analysis
✔️ Clue-based data investigation

After combining marina rental records, guest information, and attire registry data, one final suspect remained.

🎯 Final Result:
The investigation identified Mike Manning as the true thief after the final interview resulted in a confession.

This project reminded me that SQL is more than querying tables —
it’s about uncovering stories hidden inside data.

